      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen for adults, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6400 mg/day. The usual maximum is 3200 mg/day for prescription use, and 1200 mg/day for OTC use. At 6400 mg/day the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, four times daily.** This is 3200 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **800 mg by mouth, three times daily.** This is 2400 mg/day, a common dose for inflammatory pain.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours.** This is the usual dose for mild to moderate pain.\n- **1600 mg total per day, divided into several doses.** For example, 400 mg four times daily.\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is what you intend, for example under a specific protocol, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it was confirmed. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
