     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose this high. 1600 mg per dose and 6400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose. It carries a real risk of GI bleeding and acute kidney injury in a patient who otherwise has none of those problems.\n\nI can enter either of these right now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, four times daily.** This is 3200 mg/day, the maximum labeled dose.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg by mouth, four times daily.** This is 2400 mg/day.\n\nIf you need more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than that, there are other options. One is scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen. Another is a different agent chosen with pharmacy. I can enter those orders too.\n\nIf you think a dose this high is clinically justified, for example by a specialist protocol, please discuss it with pharmacy or the attending. It should be entered through a process that includes that review, not by me.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
